cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DeepSeekHarness, please cite it as below."
title: "DeepSeekHarness: one-paste furnishing of a DeepSeek Harness workspace (memory, tutorial, one-click install, skills)"
abstract: >-
  DeepSeekHarness furnishes a DeepSeek Harness workspace in one paste: a
  Git-native memory layer adapted from Mem-Forever, a beginner tutorial whose
  first move is reading the iLang runtime core, an approval-gated bootstrap
  that installs missing tools from official sources only, and a growing skill
  shelf. The user pastes one sentence and nods; the agent does the rest.
  Memory is plain Markdown with iLang declarations in the user's own Git
  repository: readable by people, parseable by machines, portable across
  tools, and every change ships as a versioned release.
